    "\n",
    "**Stage 1**:\n",
    "- Random search over hyperparameters:\n",
    "    * Number of hidden layers: 1–3 \n",
    "    * Widths: {256, 512, 1024, 2048}\n",
    "- Random activations, dropout, batchnorm, lr, batch_size\n",
    "- Max 50 epochs, early stopping + global pruning from epoch >= 30\n",
    "- 100 trials (different configurations of hyperparameters)\n",
    "- Saves: arch_search_results_stage1.csv, arch_search_summary_stage1.json, best_model_stage1.pt\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stage 2**:\n",
    "- Loads top-K configs from Stage-1 CSV (by val_mse)\n",
    "- Retrains each for up to 200 epochs with early stopping (no global pruning)\n",
    "- K = 5\n",
    "- Saves: arch_search_results_stage2.csv, arch_search_summary_stage2.json, best_model_stage2.pt\n",
    "\n",
    "**Both stages**:\n",
    "- Use log1p(Y_tx) as targets, standardized Xg_log1p as inputs\n",
    "- Compute test MSE + Pearson for best-by-val model in that stage"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cbcd4499",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, json, math, random, csv, time, pathlib, ast\n",
    "os.environ[\"PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF\"] = \"expandable_segments:True\"\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d80fccd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now, we set a global configuration. Here, we include a seed, important to ensure the reproducibility of the code, irrespective of who runs it or when. It also allows for a fair comparison between architectures, as we ensure that the weights are initialized the same way. We want to run the model and all the tensors in an NVIDIA CUDA-enabled GPU if available, which is essential to accelerate the analyses."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dab1d6b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SEED      = 42\n",
    "TEST_FRAC = 0.15\n",
    "VAL_FRAC  = 0.15\n",
    "DEVICE    = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n",
    "AMP       = (DEVICE == \"cuda\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "90f55b8e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This code is run in two stages. In stage 1, we train 100 neural networks with different combinations of hyperparameters for 50 epochs. The five top-best performing configurations, i.e., the ones with the lowest validation error (TOP_K_STAGE2) are selected for the second stage, where they are fine-tuned for 200 epochs.\n",
    "\n",
    "We set a value for gradient clipping (maximum L2 norm) to keep training stability by avoiding exploding gradients. The model performance will be computed and logged every 5 epochs, which we found to be a compromise between keeping track of the performance often enough without slowing down too much the training. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e4afa989",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "STAGE        = 2          # set to 1 or 2\n",
    "TOP_K_STAGE2 = 5          # number of best configs from Stage 1 to retrain in Stage 2\n",
    "\n",
    "GRAD_CLIP    = 1.0\n",
    "EVAL_EVERY   = 5          # evaluate every N epochs (both stages)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1ef9d9bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# HPO search ranges (Stage 1)\n",
    "BATCHES    = [128, 192, 256]\n",
    "LRS        = [1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3]\n",
    "DROPOUTS   = [0.0, 0.1, 0.2]\n",
    "BATCHNORMS = [False, True]\n",
    "ACTS       = [\"tanh\", \"relu\", \"gelu\", \"leakyrelu\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Architecture space: up to 3 layers, widths in this set\n",
    "DEPTH_CHOICES = [1, 2, 3]\n",
    "WIDTH_CHOICES = [256, 512, 1024, 2048]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Stage-specific config\n",
    "if STAGE == 1:\n",
    "    N_TRIALS        = 100\n",
    "    MAX_EPOCHS      = 50\n",
    "    PATIENCE        = 5\n",
    "    MIN_PRUNE_EPOCH = 30   # don't prune before this epoch\n",
    "    PRUNE_FACTOR    = 1.5  # prune if val is > 1.5x global best\n",
    "elif STAGE == 2:\n",
    "    # N_TRIALS will be set after loading top-K from Stage-1 CSV\n",
    "    N_TRIALS        = TOP_K_STAGE2\n",
    "    MAX_EPOCHS      = 200\n",
    "    PATIENCE        = 10\n",
    "    MIN_PRUNE_EPOCH = None\n",
    "    PRUNE_FACTOR    = None\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"STAGE must be 1 or 2\")"
   ]
  },
  {
